# PROFILES FOLDED INTO THEIR SECTION PAGE, 2026-09-01.
#
# Stephen's rule that day: a human entity is found in the AI People Directory
# or in one of its sub categories, and nowhere else. So the 58 per-person pages
# at /ai-ecosystem/ecosystem-entities-market-and-operations/{uid}/ stopped being
# published and each profile now renders inside the page for the person's
# PRIMARY category, anchored on that same uid.
#
# The uid did not change. That is exactly what the 2026-08-03 identifier rule
# was for: /.../{catUid}/#{uid} survives a rename the way /.../{uid}/ did,
# because neither address is derived from the name. Every citation of the old
# form lands on the same profile, at the anchor, in one hop.
#
# Primary category comes from twoai_person_category.is_primary, which was
# already set and already unique per person. It is stored data, not a rule
# invented at render time, because it is now an address and a rule that
# reshuffled between runs would move published URLs.
#
# The name sits on its own line ABOVE each rule, not after it. Cloudflare's
# _redirects parser reads a line as whitespace-separated tokens and stops at
# three; a trailing "# Name" is a fourth and fifth token, not a comment, and
# the 2026-09-01 deploy was rejected for it after the build had passed. A line
# that STARTS with # is a comment and costs nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 2026-09-06: THE 59 PER-PERSON REDIRECTS THAT WERE HERE ARE REMOVED. They
# sent a person's own URL to an anchor on their category page, because for
# five days a profile had no page of its own. Stephen asked for the page back:
# a person is an entity and an entity gets a URL. The pipeline writes
# people/{uid}.json again and the route renders it, so those URLs resolve to
# pages rather than redirecting. The anchor form still works - the category
# page keeps each uid as the id of its list row - so links published while the
# redirects were live land on the right person either way. Nothing 404s in
# either direction, which is the whole test.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Her entity-id stub (roster-only, unlisted, bio_len=0) was the one per-person
